      "declarations": [
        {
          "kind": "class",
          "description": "Visualize graphs, run graph algorithms step by step (BFS, DFS, Dijkstra, spanning tree, cycle detection, coloring) and record graph animations.\nThe graph, the recorded animation and the permissions are stored in the widget's data blocks. Permissions limit what readers may edit, run and replay.\n\nConversions: a `table` (edge list or square adjacency matrix) becomes a graph, and the graph becomes an adjacency matrix `table`.\nFiles: DOT (`.gv`, `.dot`) and an edge list as CSV (`.csv`), both ways. The graph is undirected, so a `digraph` is read without directions.\nFormats carry names, links and weights, not the layout or the animation; an import replaces the graph and clears the animation.\nSignals: `nodeCount` (number) and `edges` (table with columns source, target, weight).",
          "name": "WwGraph",
          "cssParts": [
            {
              "description": "The area that holds the graph.",
              "name": "graph"
            },
            {
              "description": "A node of the graph.",
              "name": "node"
            }
          ],
          "members": [
